-        {id:"FIX-120",title:"Profit Lock geometry reset at TP extension",status:"IMPLEMENTED · PRODUCTION/REPLAY TRADING-SEMANTIC CORRECTION",scenario:"A TP extension changes the entry→target geometry while an already-ACTIVE Profit Lock still carries an executable lock calculated against the superseded target. BICOUSDT #1055 proved that extension-time progress can remain barely above activation while the carried lock is still too tight for the newly-approved target.",symbol:"ALL LONG POSITIONS (primary evidence BICOUSDT #1055; original FIX-118 controls ICPUSDT #1010/#1014)",entry:"UNCHANGED",exit:"FRESH PROFIT-LOCK BASELINE AT TP GEOMETRY BOUNDARY",entryTime:"Existing position lifecycle",exitTime:"TP-extension boundary and subsequent live/replay protection",replayWindow:"Primary validation: BICOUSDT #1055 around 2026-09-07 13:25:08→13:32:09 UTC (16:25:08→16:32:09 KSA), plus ICPUSDT #1010/#1014 FIX-118 windows.",location:"DynamicProfitLockService.onTakeProfitExtended + ShadowProductionReplayService.rebaseForExtendedTarget + REBASE reactivation path",classes:["DynamicProfitLockService","ShadowProductionReplayService","DynamicProfitLockServiceTest","ShadowProductionReplayServiceFix120ParityTest","LivePositionProtectionServiceFix118RebaseTest","ProfitLockPolicy","fix-registry.js","md/FIX-120.md"],cause:"FIX-118 correctly disabled stale locks when the extended geometry immediately dropped current/highest progress below activation. But when progress remained at/above activation, the old executable lock could still be retained solely because ProfitLockPolicy is monotonic within one unchanged TP geometry. A lock calculated against TP1 is not a valid calculation baseline after continuation replaces TP1 with TP2.",solution:"Treat every approved TP extension as a Profit Lock geometry boundary. Recalculate progress against the new TP. If progress is below activation, enter/continue TP_EXTENSION_REBASE and keep the historical lock non-executable. If progress remains activation-qualified, stay ACTIVE but call the existing ProfitLockPolicy with previousActive=false and previousLock=null, using raw extensionPrice as current and extensionHighest as the previous-highest seed, so the executable lock is freshly derived from the new geometry. Apply the same fresh-baseline rule when REBASE later reactivates. Normal monotonic trailing resumes after the new baseline is established.",behavior:"Intentional narrow post-entry correction. The absolute lock may legitimately move lower or higher at a TP geometry boundary; correctness is defined by the existing ProfitLockPolicy result under the new geometry, not by monotonic comparison with the superseded lock. ProfitLockPolicy percentages/normal trailing, TP-extension qualification/formula, Stop Loss, hard floor, normal SELL authority, FIX-117 Near-TP, entry logic, sizing and FIX-119 are unchanged. Production and Replay are parity-aligned.",regression:"Exact ICP #1010/#1014 remain REBASE cases; exact BICO #1055 stays ACTIVE at ~70.129593% but receives fresh lock 0.023172519240 and does not trigger DPL at historical 0.023200; explicit lower-lock and higher-lock geometry-boundary tests; post-boundary monotonic trailing; REBASE→ACTIVE fresh-lock reactivation; repeated extension timestamp preservation; normal SELL authority during REBASE; and Production/Replay parity for ACTIVE→ACTIVE and ACTIVE→REBASE."},
-        {id:"FIX-119",title:"Accumulated-evidence late-entry timing deferral",status:"IMPLEMENTED · NARROW PRODUCTION/REPLAY ENTRY-TIMING CORRECTION",scenario:"An initial ACCUMULATED_EVIDENCE opportunity is valid enough to remain alive, but current Entry Quality is LATE_ENTRY while accumulated 1m evidence contains zero BUY observations and the fresh 5m setup is not BUY/STRONG_BUY. Historical evidence cases BTCUSDT #1701, EDUUSDT #1716 and UNIUSDT #1731 executed under this weak timing authority.",symbol:"ALL (primary evidence BTCUSDT #1701 / EDUUSDT #1716 / UNIUSDT #1731; protected controls ICPUSDT #1702 / SUIUSDT #1696)",entry:"ACCUMULATED_EVIDENCE INITIAL ENTRY ONLY",exit:"UNCHANGED",entryTime:"Production/Replay signal evaluation time",exitTime:"UNCHANGED",replayWindow:"Validate the 2026-09-06/07 KSA evidence windows and broader historical Replay for deferred/released/missed opportunities.",location:"ExecutionIntelligenceService accumulated-evidence path after the existing shared Entry Quality guard",classes:["ExecutionIntelligenceService","ExecutionIntelligenceServiceTest","fix-registry.js","md/FIX-119.md"],cause:"Entry Quality correctly classifies scores 50-54 as LATE_ENTRY, but the shared guard intentionally treats that range as a sizing warning rather than a timing block. Recent-rejection scoring is also prevented from pushing an otherwise non-chase candidate below the 50-point chase cutoff. ACCUMULATED_EVIDENCE could therefore open a WATCH-only opportunity at a price already identified as late even without accumulated BUY evidence or fresh 5m BUY authority.",solution:"After the existing shared Entry Quality guard, apply a FIX-119 guard only to already-allowed ACCUMULATED_EVIDENCE decisions. If Entry Quality is LATE_ENTRY, buyCount is zero and fresh 5m is not BUY/STRONG_BUY, return BUILDING with ACCUMULATED_LATE_ENTRY_DEFERRED while preserving the same Evidence object. Existing saveOpportunity() persistence then keeps the opportunity alive for improved geometry or fresh BUY confirmation. ACCEPTABLE_ENTRY accumulated trades and late trades with accumulated/fresh-5m BUY authority retain existing behavior.",behavior:"Intentional narrow initial-entry timing correction. It does not change Evidence/EntryQuality structures, thresholds, scoring, rejection-zone math, direct BUY validation, setup ATR authority, setup confirmation wake-up, recovery paths, progressive adds, sizing rules for still-allowed entries, exits, wallet semantics, or FIX-118/FIX-117 behavior. 1h BUY alone is not a bypass, matching EDU #1716. Production and Replay use the same shared guard.",regression:"Verify BTC/UNI late WATCH-only accumulated candidates defer to BUILDING; EDU still defers despite 1h BUY; ICP #1702 remains allowed at Entry Quality 55 ACCEPTABLE_ENTRY; SUI #1696 remains allowed with BUY evidence/fresh 5m BUY at LATE_ENTRY 50; and non-ACCUMULATED authorities remain unchanged."},
-        {id:"FIX-118",title:"Profit Lock TP-extension rebase",status:"IMPLEMENTED · PRODUCTION/REPLAY TRADING-SEMANTIC CORRECTION",scenario:"An already-earned Dynamic Profit Lock can remain executable after continuation extends TP even though progress against the wider current target falls back below the configured activation threshold. ICPUSDT #1010/#1014 proved the historical lock could terminate an otherwise approved continuation.",symbol:"ALL LONG POSITIONS (primary evidence ICPUSDT #1010 / #1014)",entry:"UNCHANGED",exit:"FIX-118 TP_EXTENSION_REBASE STATE",entryTime:"Existing position lifecycle",exitTime:"Live-price and authoritative signal-price protection",replayWindow:"Primary validation: ICPUSDT #1010 around 2026-09-06 12:58:03→13:04:30 UTC (15:58:03→16:04:30 KSA) and #1014 around 13:41:03→14:08:03 UTC (16:41:03→17:08:03 KSA).",location:"DynamicProfitLockService + LivePositionProtectionService + PaperTradingService + ShadowProductionReplayService + persisted wallet/replay state",classes:["ProfitLockState","WalletManagedPosition","DynamicProfitLockService","LivePositionProtectionService","PaperTradingService","ShadowProductionReplayService","V82__fix_118_profit_lock_tp_extension_rebase.sql","DynamicProfitLockServiceTest","LivePositionProtectionServiceTpExtensionSyncTest","fix-registry.js","md/FIX-118.md"],cause:"Profit Lock legitimately activated under the pre-extension TP geometry and remained sticky. ICPUSDT #1010/#1014 proved that when continuation widened TP enough to move current-geometry progress below activation, the historical lock could still remain executable and terminate the approved continuation.",solution:"Persist explicit INACTIVE/ACTIVE/TP_EXTENSION_REBASE state. When an ACTIVE lock falls below activation under an extended TP, keep its historical flag/price persisted but non-executable until current geometry re-earns activation. During REBASE keep Stop Loss absolute and enforce the standalone entry×1.0005 protected-profit floor. FIX-120 later