+        {id:"FIX-120",title:"Profit Lock geometry reset at TP extension",status:"IMPLEMENTED · PRODUCTION/REPLAY TRADING-SEMANTIC CORRECTION",scenario:"A TP extension changes the entry→target geometry while an already-ACTIVE Profit Lock still carries an executable lock calculated against the superseded target. BICOUSDT #1055 proved that extension-time progress can remain barely above activation while the carried lock is still too tight for the newly-approved target.",symbol:"ALL LONG POSITIONS (primary evidence BICOUSDT #1055; original FIX-118 controls ICPUSDT #1010/#1014)",entry:"UNCHANGED",exit:"FRESH PROFIT-LOCK BASELINE AT TP GEOMETRY BOUNDARY",entryTime:"Existing position lifecycle",exitTime:"TP-extension boundary and subsequent live/replay protection",replayWindow:"Primary validation: BICOUSDT #1055 around 2026-09-07 13:25:08→13:32:09 UTC (16:25:08→16:32:09 KSA), plus ICPUSDT #1010/#1014 FIX-118 windows.",location:"DynamicProfitLockService.onTakeProfitExtended + ShadowProductionReplayService.rebaseForExtendedTarget + REBASE reactivation path",classes:["DynamicProfitLockService","ShadowProductionReplayService","DynamicProfitLockServiceTest","ShadowProductionReplayServiceFix120ParityTest","LivePositionProtectionServiceFix118RebaseTest","ProfitLockPolicy","fix-registry.js","md/FIX-120.md"],cause:"FIX-118 correctly disabled stale locks when the extended geometry immediately dropped current/highest progress below activation. But when progress remained at/above activation, the old executable lock could still be retained solely because ProfitLockPolicy is monotonic within one unchanged TP geometry. A lock calculated against TP1 is not a valid calculation baseline after continuation replaces TP1 with TP2.",solution:"Treat every approved TP extension as a Profit Lock geometry boundary. Recalculate progress against the new TP. If progress is below activation, enter/continue TP_EXTENSION_REBASE and keep the historical lock non-executable. If progress remains activation-qualified, stay ACTIVE but call the existing ProfitLockPolicy with previousActive=false and previousLock=null, using raw extensionPrice as current and extensionHighest as the previous-highest seed, so the executable lock is freshly derived from the new geometry. Apply the same fresh-baseline rule when REBASE later reactivates. Normal monotonic trailing resumes after the new baseline is established.",behavior:"Intentional narrow post-entry correction. The absolute lock may legitimately move lower or higher at a TP geometry boundary; correctness is defined by the existing ProfitLockPolicy result under the new geometry, not by monotonic comparison with the superseded lock. ProfitLockPolicy percentages/normal trailing, TP-extension qualification/formula, Stop Loss, hard floor, normal SELL authority, FIX-117 Near-TP, entry logic, sizing and FIX-119 are unchanged. Production and Replay are parity-aligned.",regression:"Exact ICP #1010/#1014 remain REBASE cases; exact BICO #1055 stays ACTIVE at ~70.129593% but receives fresh lock 0.023172519240 and does not trigger DPL at historical 0.023200; explicit lower-lock and higher-lock geometry-boundary tests; post-boundary monotonic trailing; REBASE→ACTIVE fresh-lock reactivation; repeated extension timestamp preservation; normal SELL authority during REBASE; and Production/Replay parity for ACTIVE→ACTIVE and ACTIVE→REBASE."},
+        {id:"FIX-119",title:"Accumulated-evidence late-entry timing deferral",status:"IMPLEMENTED · NARROW PRODUCTION/REPLAY ENTRY-TIMING CORRECTION",scenario:"An initial ACCUMULATED_EVIDENCE opportunity is valid enough to remain alive, but current Entry Quality is LATE_ENTRY while accumulated 1m evidence contains zero BUY observations and the fresh 5m setup is not BUY/STRONG_BUY. Historical evidence cases BTCUSDT #1701, EDUUSDT #1716 and UNIUSDT #1731 executed under this weak timing authority.",symbol:"ALL (primary evidence BTCUSDT #1701 / EDUUSDT #1716 / UNIUSDT #1731; protected controls ICPUSDT #1702 / SUIUSDT #1696)",entry:"ACCUMULATED_EVIDENCE INITIAL ENTRY ONLY",exit:"UNCHANGED",entryTime:"Production/Replay signal evaluation time",exitTime:"UNCHANGED",replayWindow:"Validate the 2026-09-06/07 KSA evidence windows and broader historical Replay for deferred/released/missed opportunities.",location:"ExecutionIntelligenceService accumulated-evidence path after the existing shared Entry Quality guard",classes:["ExecutionIntelligenceService","ExecutionIntelligenceServiceTest","fix-registry.js","md/FIX-119.md"],cause:"Entry Quality correctly classifies scores 50-54 as LATE_ENTRY, but the shared guard intentionally treats that range as a sizing warning rather than a timing block. Recent-rejection scoring is also prevented from pushing an otherwise non-chase candidate below the 50-point chase cutoff. ACCUMULATED_EVIDENCE could therefore open a WATCH-only opportunity at a price already identified as late even without accumulated BUY evidence or fresh 5m BUY authority.",solution:"After the existing shared Entry Quality guard, apply a FIX-119 guard only to already-allowed ACCUMULATED_EVIDENCE decisions. If Entry Quality is LATE_ENTRY, buyCount is zero and fresh 5m is not BUY/STRONG_BUY, return BUILDING with ACCUMULATED_LATE_ENTRY_DEFERRED while preserving the same Evidence object. Existing saveOpportunity() persistence then keeps the opportunity alive for improved geometry or fresh BUY confirmation. ACCEPTABLE_ENTRY accumulated trades and late trades with accumulated/fresh-5m BUY authority retain existing behavior.",behavior:"Intentional narrow initial-entry timing correction. It does not change Evidence/EntryQuality structures, thresholds, scoring, rejection-zone math, direct BUY validation, setup ATR authority, setup confirmation wake-up, recovery paths, progressive adds, sizing rules for still-allowed entries, exits, wallet semantics, or FIX-118/FIX-117 behavior. 1h BUY alone is not a bypass, matching EDU #1716. Production and Replay use the same shared guard.",regression:"Verify BTC/UNI late WATCH-only accumulated candidates defer to BUILDING; EDU still defers despite 1h BUY; ICP #1702 remains allowed at Entry Quality 55 ACCEPTABLE_ENTRY; SUI #1696 remains allowed with BUY evidence/fresh 5m BUY at LATE_ENTRY 50; and non-ACCUMULATED authorities remain unchanged."},
+        {id:"FIX-118",title:"Profit Lock TP-extension rebase",status:"IMPLEMENTED · PRODUCTION/REPLAY TRADING-SEMANTIC CORRECTION",scenario:"An already-earned Dynamic Profit Lock can remain executable after continuation extends TP even though progress against the wider current target falls back below the configured activation threshold. ICPUSDT #1010/#1014 proved the historical lock could terminate an otherwise approved continuation.",symbol:"ALL LONG POSITIONS (primary evidence ICPUSDT #1010 / #1014)",entry:"UNCHANGED",exit:"FIX-118 TP_EXTENSION_REBASE STATE",entryTime:"Existing position lifecycle",exitTime:"Live-price and authoritative signal-price protection",replayWindow:"Primary validation: ICPUSDT #1010 around 2026-09-06 12:58:03→13:04:30 UTC (15:58:03→16:04:30 KSA) and #1014 around 13:41:03→14:08:03 UTC (16:41:03→17:08:03 KSA).",location:"DynamicProfitLockService + LivePositionProtectionService + PaperTradingService + ShadowProductionReplayService + persisted wallet/replay state",classes:["ProfitLockState","WalletManagedPosition","DynamicProfitLockService","LivePositionProtectionService","PaperTradingService","ShadowProductionReplayService","V82__fix_118_profit_lock_tp_extension_rebase.sql","DynamicProfitLockServiceTest","LivePositionProtectionServiceTpExtensionSyncTest","fix-registry.js","md/FIX-118.md"],cause:"Profit Lock legitimately activated under the pre-extension TP geometry and remained sticky. ICPUSDT #1010/#1014 proved that when continuation widened TP enough to move current-geometry progress below activation, the historical lock could still remain executable and terminate the approved continuation.",solution:"Persist explicit INACTIVE/ACTIVE/TP_EXTENSION_REBASE state. When an ACTIVE lock falls below activation under an extended TP, keep its historical flag/price persisted but non-executable until current geometry re-earns activation. During REBASE keep Stop Loss absolute and enforce the standalone entry×1.0005 protected-profit floor. FIX-120 later refines the separate at/above-activation geometry-boundary case.",behavior:"Intentional narrow exit-management correction. TP-extension eligibility/formula and configured Profit Lock percentages are unchanged. Stop Loss, normal thesis exits, FIX-117 Near-TP state/priority/thresholds, sizing and entry rules remain unchanged.",regression:"Verify ICP #1010/#1014 ACTIVE→TP_EXTENSION_REBASE when new-geometry progress falls below activation; old lock cannot trigger during rebase; reactivation occurs only after current geometry re-earns activation; standalone protected-profit floor remains available; Production and Replay keep equivalent state semantics. FIX-120 owns fresh-lock baseline regression when extension progress remains at/above activation."},
+        {id:"FIX-117",title:"Preserve earned Near-TP protection across TP extension",status:"IMPLEMENTED · NARROW PRODUCTION/REPLAY POSITION-PROTECTION CORRECTION",scenario:"An already-open long position has earned FIX-11T Near-TP protection, then reaches TP and PositionContinuationPolicy legitimately extends the target. Before FIX-117 the extension erased the earned state and forced re-arming against the wider target.",symbol:"ALL LONG POSITIONS (evidence case ENAUSDT #978)",entry:"UNCHANGED",exit:"EXISTING FIX-11T HARVEST AUTHORITY ONLY",entryTime:"Existing position lifecycle",exitTime:"Live price / Replay price-event time",replayWindow:"Use ENAUSDT 2026-09-05 around 18:20:52→18:49:13 UTC (21:20:52→21:49:13 KSA) for the primary evidence case.",location:"LivePositionProtectionService TP-extension state reset + ShadowProductionReplayService ShadowPosition.withTakeProfit()",classes:["LivePositionProtectionService","ShadowProductionReplayService","Fix117NearTpExtensionStateTest","NearTpFailureProtectionPolicyTest","md/FIX-117.md"],cause:"TP extension unconditionally reset all unharvested Near-TP state to INACTIVE, deleting protection already earned against the prior target. ENAUSDT #978 armed above 90% of the original TP distance, then continuation extended TP and erased the state; the wider target was never re-armed before the later reversal.",solution:"Preserve NEAR_TP_ARMED state and historical best price across TP extension. Preserve NEAR_TP_REJECTION_DETECTED and best price but clear bearish streak/last 1m evidence accumulated under the old geometry. Keep INACTIVE and NEAR_TP_FAILURE_CONFIRMED on the existing reset behavior; preserve terminal PARTIAL_HARVESTED behavior. Apply identical semantics in Replay.",behavior:"Intentional, narrow post-entry Production/Replay correction. It does not change entry qualification, BUY/SELL thresholds, continuation eligibility, the 90% arm threshold, 20% giveback threshold, two-1m/fresh-5m confirmation rule, 50% harvest size, Binance minimum guard, normal exit policy, stop loss, or Dynamic Profit Lock. It only prevents an earned FIX-11T state from being erased by a later TP extension.",regression:"Verify ARMED preservation; REJECTION_DETECTED immediate preservation with evidence reset; recovery when recalculated giveback falls below 20%; continued rejection when giveback remains at least 20%; INACTIVE reset unchanged; FAILURE_CONFIRMED reset unchanged; Production/Replay parity; and all existing NearTpFailureProtectionPolicy tests unchanged."},
+        {id:"FIX-11T",title:"Production + Replay Near-TP failure protection partial harvest",status:"IMPLEMENTED · CONTROLLED PRODUCTION BEHAVIOR CHANGE",scenario:"An already-open long position reaches at least 90% of its planned entry→TP distance, then gives back at least 20%. The system observes the rejection and only reduces exposure after persistent fresh 1m underlying SELL/STRONG_SELL evidence while fresh 5m original BUY/STRONG_BUY support is absent.",symbol:"ALL LONG POSITIONS",entry:"UNCHANGED",exit:"ONE 50% PARTIAL HARVEST AFTER CONFIRMED NEAR-TP FAILURE",entryTime:"Existing position lifecycle",exitTime:"Live price / Replay price-event time",replayWindow:"Replay uses the same shared NearTpFailureProtectionPolicy. Exact-price Replay uses persisted market_price_event ordering; legacy signal-price fallback uses the same rule on authoritative historical signal prices.",location:"LivePositionProtectionService + ShadowProductionReplayService + shared NearTpFailureProtectionPolicy",classes:["NearTpFailureProtectionPolicy","NearTpState","LivePositionProtectionService","WalletAutoExecutionService","BinanceMinimumExecutionPolicy","BinanceMarketDataClient","WalletManagedPosition","WalletTradeRepository","PaperTradingService","ShadowProductionReplayService","V81__near_tp_failure_protection.sql","NearTpFailureProtectionPolicyTest","md/FIX-11T.md"],cause:"Near-TP winners can reverse into losses, but historical controls proved that proximity or giveback alone is too aggressive. Missing/stale evidence must never be treated as bearish confirmation, one noisy 1m SELL is insufficient, and a real partial sell must survive restart/retry without duplicate execution or immediate progressive re-buy.",solution:"Arm at 90% TP progress; detect but do not sell on 20% giveback; reset rejection when price recovers inside the same 20% boundary; require two distinct fresh 1m original SELL/STRONG_SELL signals plus fresh 5m evidence whose original decision is no longer BUY/STRONG_BUY; then request one idempotent 50% partial reduction of CURRENT held quantity. Before wallet mutation, compare the requested order notional with the symbol's current Binance NOTIONAL/MIN_NOTIONAL floor from exchangeInfo. If it is below the Binance minimum, or the minimum cannot be obtained safely, execute nothing and continue normal management; never promote the partial harvest to a larger/full sell. Persist position state, best price, bearish streak, last evaluated 1m signal and actual harvested quantity. Keep cumulative allocatedPositionPercent unchanged so future progressive targets permanently reserve the harvested exposure gap.",behavior:"Intentional Production behavior change after entry only. BUY qualification, trade frequency, entry sizing, existing TP/SL/profit-lock/normal exit authority and their priority remain unchanged. Near-TP runs last and cannot act on missing/stale evidence. Production and Replay also share the Binance minimum-executable-notional guard; a below-minimum 50% harvest is skipped with an explicit server log and the position continues unchanged. Remaining quantity continues under existing management. The partial SELL remains in the wallet ledger/realized-P&L truth but is excluded from CLOSED-position queries so it cannot masquerade as a completed trade. Replay executes the same shared policy and records partial SELL/P&L without closing the shadow position.",regression:"Verify missing/stale 1m/5m never harvests; a single bearish 1m does not harvest; two distinct fresh bearish 1m signals plus lost 5m support can confirm; fresh 5m BUY/STRONG_BUY blocks; recovery inside the 20% rejection boundary resets persistence; TP extension/progressive add resets pre-harvest Near-TP geometry; duplicate execution key cannot sell twice; paper_position quantity/P&L stays synchronized; Replay exact/fallback paths preserve partial proceeds/P&L and keep the position open."},
+        {id:"FIX-11S",title:"Replay window all-trades chart with Production overlay",status:"IMPLEMENTED · OBSERVABILITY ONLY",scenario:"Review every split Replay BUY/SELL execution for one run on a single chart and optionally compare real Production executions for the same symbol/window.",symbol:"ALL",entry:"DISPLAY ONLY",exit:"DISPLAY ONLY",entryTime:"Replay run window",exitTime:"Replay run window",replayWindow:"Uses the exact analysis_test_run start_time → end_time.",location:"Proven Analysis / Replay run chart",classes:["RegressionTestService","RegressionTestController","proven-analyzed-trades.html","proven-analyzed-trades.js","administration.css","md/FIX-11S.md"],cause:"Per-position charts made split executions and Replay-vs-Production timing divergence difficult to inspect together.",solution:"Add a run-level chart payload with every wallet_execution_test BUY/SELL plus optional wallet_trade Production BUY/SELL rows for the same symbol/window. Production rows are always an empty array when none exist. UI draws separate Replay and Production BUY→SELL trade-path lines in distinct colors, omits R_BUY/R_SELL/P_BUY/P_SELL text markers, and keeps a Show Production toggle.",behavior:"Read-only UI/reporting only. No Production or Replay analysis, decision, execution, sizing, wallet, threshold, position-management or exit behavior changes.",regression:"Verify runs with both sources, Replay-only runs with zero Production executions, Production-only windows, zero-execution windows, split BUY/SELL path linking, separation between fully closed positions, interval switching, and Production hide/show without chart failure."},
